From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:10:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] H12: named properties through shared and inherited
 resources

A form whose /Resources is the page's resources object, or that has no
/Resources, or a direct one without /Properties, drew text marked with an
OFF optional-content group named only in the page's /Properties.

Two causes. hayro-syntax's cycle guard refuses any object already on the
lookup's parent chain, so a form reached through object 5 could not
resolve /Resources 5 0 R and got empty resources; fonts and nested forms
hid this because their getters walk the inherited chain. And the BDC
handler read only the innermost /Properties.

Resources::resolve_dict looks a referenced /Resources up afresh; forms,
Type 3 fonts and glyph procedures, and tiling patterns use it. The guard
itself is unchanged. Resources::get_property and get_property_ref walk
the parent chain like the other getters, and the BDC handler walks it
level by level through the per-dictionary property cache.

Corpus C gains the three leaking shapes and four controls, all exact.
